NAME
       init - first process, starts consoles and the graphical session

SYNOPSIS
       /sbin/init

DESCRIPTION
       The kernel starts init as PID 1. init reads /etc/inittab, starts the
       listed programs and reaps every orphaned process.

       Each line of /etc/inittab is

           id:action:command arguments

       and lines starting with # are comments. Actions:

       sysinit, wait
           run the command and wait for it to finish
       once
           run the command once
       respawn
           run the command and start it again whenever it exits
           (paused for 10 seconds when it dies 5 times within 2 seconds)
       graphical
           like once, skipped when the kernel command line contains text,
           single, nogui or 3

       Without /etc/inittab init runs getty on tty1-tty6 and /sbin/startgui.

KERNEL COMMAND LINE
       text
           stay on the text consoles, do not start graphics
       gui=kernel
           the kernel starts the desktop itself during boot
       verbose, loglevel=7
           keep printing all kernel messages on tty1 after login starts;
           by default only warnings and errors are shown there

FILES
       /etc/inittab, /proc/cmdline

SEE ALSO
       getty(8), startgui(8), chvt(1)
